<td id="S2.T1.5.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">24</td>
<td id="S2.T1.5.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">8</td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Vulnerability Collection and Processing.</span>
To comprehensively study vulnerabilities within the LLMSC, we aggregated data from a diverse set of sources, including official databases such as MITRE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a>]</cite> and GitHub Advisory <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>]</cite>, and bounty platforms like huntr <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">36</a>]</cite>. Using each package’s repository name as our primary query key, we initially collected a total of 7,151 vulnerability records—4,796 from the MITRE CVE list, 567 from the GitHub Advisory database, and 1,788 from huntr, an open-source, crowd-sourced disclosure platform specializing in AI/ML vulnerabilities.
After collecting the raw data, we processed it through three major filtering steps, as summarized in <a href="#S2.T1" title="TABLE I ‣ II-A Dataset Collection and Pre-process ‣ II Dataset and Supply Chain Construction ‣ Understanding Large Language Model Supply Chain: Structure, Domain, and Vulnerabilities" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table I</span></a>. First, we applied deduplication filters to remove redundant records within and across sources, resulting in a reduction of 387 records from huntr, 23 records from GitHub Advisory, and 2,330 records from MITRE. Second, we evaluated the relevance of each vulnerability to the LLMSC ecosystem by cross-checking repository associations and filtering out unrelated entries. This step excluded an additional 1,253 records from huntr, 520 from GitHub Advisory, and 2,458 from MITRE.
Finally, after completing deduplication and relevance filtering, we derived a curated dataset containing 180 vulnerabilities: 148 from huntr, 24 from GitHub Advisory, and 8 from MITRE.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S2.SS2.6" class="ltx_text">II-B</span> </span><span id="S2.SS2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">LLM Supply Chain Construction</span></h3>

<div id="S2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The LLMSC is conceptualized and structured as a directed graph to effectively capture the intricate relationships within the LLM software ecosystem. In this graph, nodes represent individual software packages or vulnerabilities, while directed edges signify either dependency relationships between packages or the impact of vulnerabilities on their corresponding packages. Formally, we define the LLMSC as a directed graph <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=\langle V_{\text{from}},V_{\text{to}},E\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>from</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>to</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=\langle V_{\text{from}},V_{\text{to}},E\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\text{from}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>from</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\text{from}}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the set of upstream software packages, serving as foundational or prerequisite components, and <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\text{to}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>to</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\text{to}}</annotation></semantics></math> symbolizes the set of downstream software packages that depend on these upstream packages. The set <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E\subseteq V_{\text{from}}\times V_{\text{to}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>from</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>to</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E\subseteq V_{\text{from}}\times V_{\text{to}}</annotation></semantics></math> comprises directed edges, each indicating a dependency relationship. Specifically, an edge <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(v_{\text{from}},v_{\text{to}})\in E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mtext>from</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mtext>to</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(v_{\text{from}},v_{\text{to}})\in E</annotation></semantics></math> indicates that the downstream package <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{\text{to}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mtext>to</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{\text{to}}</annotation></semantics></math> explicitly depends on or imports functionality from the upstream package <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{\text{from}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mtext>from</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{\text{from}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span>LLMSC Construction Algorithm</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.4.1" class="ltx_listingline">




<span id="alg1.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">// </span><span id="alg1.4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">Structured as (package, version) tuples<span id="alg1.4.1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span></span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.4.2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="alg1.4.2.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="alg1.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> </span>Local dataset <math id="alg1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> , API endpoints <math id="alg1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="alg1.4.3" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="alg1.4.3.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="alg1.4.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> </span>Constructed dependency graph <math id="alg1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}=(V,E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}=(V,E)</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="alg1.4.4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.4.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1</span></span>
            <math id="alg1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\leftarrow\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\leftarrow\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E\leftarrow\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E\leftarrow\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="alg1.4.5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.4.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">2</span></span>
            <span id="alg1.4.5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">foreach</span> <em id="alg1.4.5.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="alg1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(package,version)\in\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(package,version)\in\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="alg1.4.5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.4.6" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.4.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">3</span></span>
            <math id="alg1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\leftarrow V\cup\text{CreateNode}(package,version)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mtext>CreateNode</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\leftarrow V\cup\text{CreateNode}(package,version)</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="alg1.4.7" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="alg1.4.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">// </span><span id="alg1.4.7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">Dependency resolution workflow<span id="alg1.4.7.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span></span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.4.8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.4.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">4</span></span>
            <span id="alg1.4.8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Function</span> <em id="alg1.4.8.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">ProcessDependencies(<math id="alg1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math>)</em><span id="alg1.4.8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">:</span>
